      "hints": [
        "Set discriminant $\\Delta = b^2 - 4ac = 0$: $(10m)^2 - 4(1 + m^2)(9) = 0$.",
        "Expand and simplify: $100m^2 - 36 - 36m^2 = 0 \\implies 64m^2 = 36$.",
        "Solve for $m$: $m^2 = \\dfrac{36}{64} = \\dfrac{9}{16} \\implies m = \\pm \\dfrac{3}{4}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Substitution removes y; a repeated root imposes tangency.\nSet the discriminant to zero for tangency:\n$$\\Delta = (10m)^2 - 4(1 + m^2)(9) = 0$$\n$$100m^2 - 36(1 + m^2) = 0$$\n$$100m^2 - 36m^2 - 36 = 0$$",
        "Solve for $m$:\n$$64m^2 = 36 \\implies m^2 = \\dfrac{36}{64} = \\dfrac{9}{16}$$\n$$m = \\dfrac{3}{4} \\quad \\text{or} \\quad m = -\\dfrac{3}{4}$$"
